    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a gauntlet of elite arms today, but our lineup remains optimized for efficiency in the face of tough matchups. **Kyle Tucker** (75.13) and **Andy Pages** (72.13) lead our offensive outlook, both benefiting from a favorable matchup against Brandon Pfaadt. **Andy Pages** specifically stands out as a high-upside play; while he holds a respectable base projection, the combination of a positive park factor and a slow pitcher delivery\u2014which significantly boosts his stolen base potential\u2014vaults him into our top tier. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (68.96) remains a core pillar, drawing enough of a wind advantage and lineup order projection to offset the moderate challenge of Aaron Nola.\n\nWe are navigating several high-stakes scenarios involving elite opposing pitching. **Gunnar Henderson** (61.80) faces the formidable Jacob deGrom, yet his elite lead-off status and positional versatility keep him in the green, despite the heavy penalty for deGrom's dominance. Conversely, we are banking on **Luis Robert Jr.** (62.19) for his explosive speed profile; even with a platoon disadvantage against Bubba Chandler, his ability to capitalize on a 100% stolen base-friendly delivery makes him a superior UTIL start. **Dominic Smith** was the closest player to cracking the starting lineup with a 46.70 score, but he ultimately remained on the bench because he lacks the multi-category upside that **Liam Hicks** or **Nasim Nunez** provide in their respective slots, especially given the scarcity of speed in our current roster composition.\n\nRisk management remains at the forefront, as most of our lineup is currently \"Lineup Pending.\" While we have modeled these projections assuming standard historical order, any movement in the batting order\u2014particularly for **Heliot Ramos** and **Jackson Merrill**\u2014could shift their utility. We are also wary of the heavy usage of elite arms like Chris Sale and Gerrit Cole against **Heliot Ramos** and **Drake Baldwin** respectively. While **Drake Baldwin** (56.33) is buoyed by favorable wind and a decent spot in the order, the skill gap against Cole remains our primary exposure today. We will continue to monitor the final lineups to ensure these efficiency scores hold firm before first pitch.",
